Q: VS Code, HTML autocomplete, single quotes instead of double quotes A: <p>This may be late, but I think the answer by Mark in the post &quot;<a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/55897377/how-to-make-vscode-autocomplete-html-tags-attribute-with-single-quote">How to make vscode autocomplete HTML tag's attribute with single quote?</a>&quot; has the answer you needed then.</p>
<p>Basically, since VSCode <code>v1.62</code> you are allowed to use this Emmet settings option that will autocomplete tags with attributes using single quotes:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>  &quot;emmet.syntaxProfiles&quot;: {
    &quot;html&quot;: {
      &quot;attr_quotes&quot;: &quot;single&quot;,
    },
  },
</code></pre>
<p>That worked for me, I hope it helps.</p>
